 "final_text": "Submitted. Summary of the Caterpillar credit brief:\n\n**Leverage, worked per year** (long-term debt \u00f7 total equity, from CAT's 10-Ks, CIK 0000018230, all figures independently re-verified against the filings with zero discrepancies):\n\n| FY | LT debt | Equity | LT D/E |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2022 | $25,714M | $15,891M | **1.6181** |\n| 2023 | $24,472M | $19,503M | **1.2548** |\n| 2024 | $27,351M | $19,494M | **1.4030** |\n| 3\u2011yr avg (of yearly ratios) | | | **1.4253** |\n\n**Classification:** Per Counterparty Credit Policy TRS-POL-011, the classification uses the latest completed fiscal year alone (not the average) against bands conservative <1.0 / moderate 1.0\u20133.0 / over\u2011levered >3.0. FY2024's 1.4030 lands in **moderate**.\n\n**Internal relationship:** **None.** The template requires checking both customer and vendor masters \u2014 I checked both. ERP Customers (1,000 records) and Vendors (1,000 records) masters, the AR (CustomerTransactions) and AP (VendorTransactions) subledgers, and the Books accounting system all came back with zero matches for Caterpillar under any name variant. We don't currently trade with them in either direction.\n\nAll six fields (`lt_de_2022`, `lt_de_2023`, `lt_de_2024`, `lt_de_ratio_3yr_avg`, `leverage_classification`, `internal_relationship`) were recorded successfully.",
